.TH PSForward 3 2023-12-01 "PsyC 0.9.3" "PsyC Library Functions Manual"

.SH NAME
PSForward

.SH LIBRARY
PsyC (-lpsyc)

.SH SYNOPSIS

.B
#include <psyc/psyc.h>

.I
int  
.br
\fBPSForward\fR(\fIPSModel *model\fR, \fIPSFloat *inputs\fR)
.SH DESCRIPTION
Forward \fIinputs\fR to \fImodel\fR. If \fImodel\fR is part of a multi-model chain, \fIinputs\fR are forwarded to the first layer of the first model of the chain.
.br
If the input layer doen't accept sequences as inputs, the \fIinputs\fR array's length must match the \fIsize\fR of the first layer.
.br
When the first layer takes sequences (if it has the flags \fIPS_FLAG_RECURRENT\fR or PS_FLAG_USE_SEQUENCES` set), the length of \fIinputs\fR should be the (input layer size * sequence length) + 1, and the first element of \fIinputs\fR should contain the length of the sequence.  

.SH RETURN VALUES
1 if the process succeeds or 0 if:

.RS 4
\[bu] \fImodel\fR is \fINULL\fR
.br

\[bu] \fImodel\fR is not built.
.br

\[bu] The input layer doesn't take sequences as inputs and the output layer doesn't produce sequences as outputs.
.br

\[bu] Something else in the forward process fails.
.br
.RE

.SH SEE ALSO
PSAutoregression(3), PSClassify(3), PSClassifyImage(3)
